---
import Base from "../../layouts/Base.astro";
---

<Base
  title="United for Peace"
  description="How Rotaract Europe asks clubs to support Lebanon, Gaza, and Ukraine."
>
  <main id="content" class="wrap">
    <header class="page-head">
      <p class="kicker">Impact</p>
      <h1>United for Peace</h1>
      <p>
        Donation buttons on the current site are run by the clubs and agencies collecting the money. This preview links back to those pages so nothing is lost before the domain moves.
      </p>
      <p><a href="https://rotaracteurope.eu/impact/unite-for-peace/">Open the current appeals, with their donation links</a></p>
    </header>
    <article class="office">
      <h2>Lebanon</h2>
      <p>Clubs in Lebanon are collecting food, shelter, medical aid, and supplies for displaced families. The current page puts the number of people forced from their homes above 700,000.</p>
    </article>
    <article class="office">
      <h2>Gaza</h2>
      <p>The page carries the Rotary Peace Fellows’ call for a cease-fire, protection of civilians, return of hostages, and humanitarian access, and points to UNRWA’s call for funding.</p>
    </article>
    <article class="office">
      <h2>Ukraine</h2>
      <p>The appeal says food and medicine are still short, and that donations have fallen since the start of the war while the need has not.</p>
    </article>
    <h2>Peace conferences</h2>
    <div class="year">
      <strong>2025</strong>
      <p>Pompeii, with Rotaract Mediterranean. Participants worked through needs assessment, planning, alliances, resources, sustainability, and evaluation. Speakers included Patricia Shafer and Ambassador Walter B. Gyger.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="year">
      <strong>2024</strong>
      <p>Online, 20 April. Women and young people in peacebuilding. Speakers included Phill Gittins and Foteini Papadimou.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="year">
      <strong>2022</strong>
      <p>Sarajevo, 12 March. The first joint conference of the two multi-district organisations. Speakers included Dr Peter Neuner, Bilal Al Ayoubi, and Marwa Abou Dayya.</p>
    </div>
  </main>
</Base>
